  "live_records": {
    "q-9675": {
      "dom_id": "step-q9675",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the real solutions to the equation $5\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5.$",
      "worked_solution": "The definitions of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definitions into the equation  $5\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}))-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x} & =5 \\\\ 2{e}^{x}+3{e}^{-x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (2{e}^{x}+3{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}+3 & =5{e}^{x} \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}-5{e}^{x}+3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in ${e}^{x}$ that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{e}^{x}-3)({e}^{x}-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n2{e}^{x}-3=0,\\,{e}^{x}-1=0\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{x}-3 & =0 &  & \\, & {e}^{x}-1 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\frac{3}{2} &  & \\, & {e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) &  & \\, & x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=0$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})$ are the real solutions to the equation.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
