    "q-138673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138673",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definition into the equation $5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot (\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}) & =4 \\\\ 5({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =4({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\ 5{e}^{x}-5{e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{x}+4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x} & =9{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x}$ and solve the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 9{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{2x} & =9 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{1/2}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only real solution is $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
