    "q-342996": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342996",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $8\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definition into the equation $8\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}) & =1 \\\\ 8({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}+{e}^{-x} \\\\ 8{e}^{x}-8{e}^{-x} & ={e}^{x}+{e}^{-x} \\\\ 7{e}^{x} & =9{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x}$ and solve the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot 7{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 9{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{2x} & =\\frac{9}{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}) \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only real solution is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
