    "q-343010": {
      "dom_id": "step-q343010",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=7.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The definitions of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definitions into the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})+\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x} & =7 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =7 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)$ is the only real solution to the equation.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
